# Chapter Four — the Gardens.
# Question: why did the Festival of Lanterns stop?
# Beat: three years, three reasons, and one of them wearing a very good coat.

@node ch4_garden_open
  The Gardens are the worst of it. Everywhere else the gray looks like weather.
  Here it looks like something went wrong.
  A man in a wide hat is watering a bed of pencil-coloured flowers with great
  care, which is either very sad or very hopeful and is in fact both.

@node sage_intro
  [if flag ch4.met_sage == 0]
  SAGE(sad): They came up gray. I want you to know that I did everything
  right and they came up gray.
  YOU:
    * (kind) I believe you. That is not your fault.  -> sage_kind
    * (curious) Have they ever done that before?  -> sage_before
    * (dry) You are still watering them.  -> sage_water
  [else]
  goto sage_after
  [end]

@node sage_kind
  SAGE(moved): ...Thank you. My brother-in-law thinks I have lost my touch.
  My brother-in-law grows onions.
  trust sage 1
  goto sage_before

@node sage_water
  SAGE(worried): Well. Yes. They are still thirsty. Being gray has not made
  them not thirsty.
  trust sage 1
  goto sage_before

@node sage_before
  set ch4.met_sage = 1
  SAGE: Never. Not in my time and not in the book my mother kept.
  grant clue.garden_gray
  SAGE(worried): And I will tell you the other thing that has never happened
  in my time, which is three springs with no lanterns on that green.
  YOU:
    * (curious) Three. What happened each year?  -> sage_three
    * (kind) You counted them. You have been keeping count.  -> sage_count
    * (dry) Three is a habit, not an accident.  -> sage_three

@node sage_count
  SAGE(sad): You cannot not count. It is the same week every year. You look
  up on the Friday and there is nothing on the hill.
  trust sage 1
  goto sage_three

@node sage_three
  SAGE: The first year it rained. Rained like the end of something, all week.
  Nobody's fault.
  SAGE(worried): The second year there was a row about the money. I did not
  follow it. The council said it was postponed.
  SAGE(sad): The third year nobody said anything at all. That is the one that
  frightens me. Nobody even argued.
  grant clue.three_years
  SAGE(happy): Now. If you want the rest of the Gardens to talk to you, the
  rill has to run. Half my beds have been dry a fortnight.
  start_puzzle water_flow
  SAGE(moved): Look at that. Water where water goes.
  set ch4.sage_done = 1
  trust sage 1

@node sage_after
  [if flag ch4.sage_done == 1]
  SAGE: Ask Poppy. Half this town has been in her shop this year and she is
  the only one who knows why.
  [else]
  SAGE: The rill, first, if you would.
  goto sage_three
  [end]

@node poppy_intro
  [if flag ch4.met_poppy == 0]
  POPPY(neutral): You are sleeping badly. It is in your face.
  YOU:
    * (dry) It is in my job.  -> poppy_job
    * (kind) So are half the people in here, by the look of it.  -> poppy_half
    * (curious) Is everyone sleeping badly?  -> poppy_half
  [else]
  goto poppy_after
  [end]

@node poppy_job
  POPPY(laughing): It is in your job and your face. Sit down.
  goto poppy_half

@node poppy_half
  set ch4.met_poppy = 1
  POPPY(worried): Everyone. I have made more sleeping tea this year than in
  the eight before it, and more of the other kind, the getting-up kind.
  grant clue.town_lowspirits
  POPPY: It is not an illness. Low spirits are not an illness. But they are a
  fact, and facts take tea.
  YOU:
    * (curious) When did it start?  -> poppy_when
    * (kind) Including you?  -> poppy_you
    * (dry) You could bottle it and call it Prismbrook.  -> poppy_when

@node poppy_you
  POPPY(moved): ...Including me. There. I have said it to a stranger. That
  will be threepence.
  trust poppy 1
  goto poppy_when

@node poppy_when
  POPPY: Two springs back. Right about when the hill stopped having lights on
  it, since you are going to make me say it.
  POPPY(shifty): And there is one customer I will mention because he is not
  ill and he is not sleeping and he will not tell me why.
  YOU:
    * (curious) The Mayor.  -> poppy_mayor
    * (kind) You are worried about him.  -> poppy_worried
    * (dry) Let me guess. Very good coat.  -> poppy_mayor

@node poppy_worried
  POPPY(sad): I am worried about all of them. He is just the loudest about
  being fine.
  goto poppy_mayor

@node poppy_mayor
  POPPY: The Mayor. Twice a week. And every single time, if the tower comes
  up, he remembers an appointment.
  grant clue.mayor_dodges
  POPPY(happy): Now. You want my whole opinion, you can make the tea while I
  give it. Exactly the recipe. It is not a suggestion.
  start_puzzle mix_ratio
  POPPY(moved): Good. Most people guess. You counted.
  POPPY: My whole opinion is this. Nothing is wrong with this town that a
  hundred people standing on a hill together would not fix.
  set ch4.poppy_done = 1
  trust poppy 1

@node poppy_after
  [if flag ch4.poppy_done == 1]
  POPPY: Mo keeps the hives past the hedge. Mo will tell you the bees
  remember the festival. Mo is not being whimsical. I have checked.
  [else]
  POPPY: The tea, first.
  goto poppy_mayor
  [end]

@node mo_intro
  [if flag ch4.met_mo == 0]
  MO(happy): Stand still a moment. They are deciding about you.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Take your time.  -> mo_still
    * (curious) Deciding what?  -> mo_still
    * (dry) I will try to be uncontroversial.  -> mo_still
  [else]
  goto mo_after
  [end]

@node mo_still
  set ch4.met_mo = 1
  MO(laughing): There. You are furniture. Well done.
  MO: Now. You are here about the hill.
  MO(worried): I will tell you something and you will decide whether I am a
  crank, and I have made my peace with that.
  YOU:
    * (kind) I have heard stranger and believed it.  -> mo_believe
    * (curious) Go on.  -> mo_dance
    * (dry) I reserve the right to think you are a crank.  -> mo_dance

@node mo_believe
  MO(moved): ...Right. Good. Right.
  trust mo 1
  goto mo_dance

@node mo_dance
  MO: The bees dance where the good things are. That is not folklore, that is
  just what they do.
  MO(worried): Mine still dance a path over the hedge, left at nothing at
  all, and up the hill to the green. Every summer. To a green with nothing on
  it for three years.
  YOU:
    * (curious) They are dancing to something that is not there.  -> mo_notthere
    * (kind) They are remembering.  -> mo_notthere
    * (dry) Bees with a long memory and poor judgement.  -> mo_notthere

@node mo_notthere
  MO(sad): They are dancing to a night with a hundred lanterns on it. Warm
  and sweet and full of people. The best night of their year for as long as
  there have been hives here.
  MO(happy): Come and read it yourself. They will show you if you watch. Then
  you walk it back and they will know you meant it.
  start_puzzle hex_path
  MO(moved): There. Now you know the way to the festival, and so do they, and
  so does nobody else in this town.
  grant clue.bees_remember
  MO: And since you will ask. The lanterns are not lost. Nothing in
  Prismbrook is ever lost, it is only put away by somebody being tidy about
  a feeling.
  MO: They are in the shed on Tower Green. All hundred and eleven, wicks
  trimmed, waiting like an argument nobody finished.
  grant clue.lanterns_stored
  set ch4.mo_done = 1
  trust mo 1

@node mo_after
  [if flag ch4.mo_done == 1]
  MO: You are going up the hill next, and you should. Everything about this
  is up the hill.
  [else]
  MO: Watch the dance first.
  goto mo_dance
  [end]
